      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SHINELIKETHESUN (5) had been building to a win and it arrived last start when she raced parked but proved too strong by 5.5 metres at Shepparton. Her best results have come at this distance range. Could strike again. MOONSHINE LOUIE (8) continued his consistent form when he came from a wide barrier for second at Shepparton last week, making it 10 top-four finishes in succession. Can settle just behind them and wait on the sprint lane. Big chance. KYVALLEY REEVA NZ (9) was back from a let-up and came from a wide barrier for a respectable second at her most recent appearance at this circuit and distance. Can progress off that. DANCE FIGHTER (6) draws wide but cannot be left out after solid recent performances including a Maryborough win last month along with a second from this barrier.",
